description: Push workflow. Follow Conventional Commits for all messages, branch names, and PR titles. 1) Check git status on current branch, create smart commits. 2) Update CHANGELOG-NEW.md (version from composer.json, today's date, commit messages); commit. 3) If README-affected (composer.json, package.json, Dockerfile, docker-compose.yml), commit. 4) Push: If on develop (protected) → create integration branch (CC-style, e.g. feat/scope-description), push it, create/update PR to develop. If on any other branch → push directly to origin (branch not protected). 5) Do not merge; user merges manually after CI/tests pass.
alwaysApply: false
